## ♿ Accessibility Guidelines

### MUST FOLLOW: ARIA Labels
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Accessible button
<IconButton
  aria-label="Delete item"
  onClick={handleDelete}
>
  <DeleteIcon />
</IconButton>

// ✅ CORRECT: Accessible form
<TextField
  label="Search"
  inputProps={{ 'aria-describedby': 'search-helper-text' }}
/>
<FormHelperText id="search-helper-text">
  Enter keywords to search
</FormHelperText>
```

### MUST FOLLOW: Keyboard Navigation
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Provide visible focus indicators
- Implement logical tab order

### MUST FOLLOW: Color Contrast
- Ensure minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for text
- Don't rely solely on color to convey information
- Provide alternative text for images

## 🚫 Anti-Patterns

### NEVER DO: Common Mistakes
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG: Inline styles instead of sx
<div style={{ marginTop: '20px' }}>

// ❌ WRONG: Hardcoded breakpoints
@media (max-width: 768px) { ... }

// ❌ WRONG: Non-semantic HTML
<div onClick={handleClick}>Click me</div>

// ❌ WRONG: Missing accessibility
<img src="chart.png" />

// ❌ WRONG: Inconsistent spacing
<Box sx={{ mt: '15px', mb: '25px' }}>

// ❌ WRONG: Font weight not in system
<Typography sx={{ fontWeight: 450 }}>

// ❌ WRONG: Creating styled components in render
function Component() {
  const StyledDiv = styled('div')({ color: 'red' });
  return <StyledDiv />;
}
```

### NEVER DO: Performance Issues
- ❌ Don't create styled components inside render functions
- ❌ Don't use heavy animations on mobile
- ❌ Don't load large images without optimization
- ❌ Don't render large lists without virtualization
- ❌ Don't load unnecessary font weights

