### ALWAYS DO These UI Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS: Use Material-UI sx prop
<Box sx={{ color: 'primary.main', p: 2 }}>Content</Box>

// ✅ ALWAYS: Use React refs for DOM access
const chartRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

// ✅ ALWAYS: Use theme colors
const theme = useTheme();
const color = theme.palette.primary.main;

// ✅ ALWAYS: Implement responsive design
<Grid container spacing={2}>
  <Grid item xs={12} md={6}>
    Content
  </Grid>
</Grid>

// ✅ ALWAYS: Wrap components in error boundaries
<ErrorBoundary>
  <ChartComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// ✅ ALWAYS: Clean up chart instances
useEffect(() => {
  const chart = echarts.init(ref.current);
  return () => chart.dispose();
}, []);
```

## 📊 ACCESSIBILITY PATTERNS

### Accessible Chart Pattern (MUST IMPLEMENT)
```typescript
// Example: AccessibleChart.tsx
const AccessibleChart: React.FC<IChartProps> = ({ data, options }) => {
  const chartOptions: EChartsOption = {
    ...options,
    aria: {
      enabled: true,
      decal: {
        show: true,
      },
    },
  };

  return (
    <Box>
      <VisuallyHidden>
        <table>
          <caption>Chart data representation</caption>
          {/* Render data as table for screen readers */}
        </table>
      </VisuallyHidden>
      
      <BaseChart 
        data={data} 
        options={chartOptions}
        aria-label="Interactive chart"
      />
    </Box>
  );
};
```

---

**Key Principles**: 
1. Always use Material-UI components and theming system
2. Implement proper responsive design patterns
3. Follow accessibility guidelines for charts and forms
4. Use consistent color palettes and design tokens
5. Implement proper cleanup for chart instances
6. Always wrap components in error boundaries

